% Monoid axioms (associativity + right-identity, no inverse).
% Conjecture: applying the right-identity to a specific term
% reduces it.  Proves trivially via a single rewrite of the
% right-identity rule.
NAME            monoid_right_id
MODE            PROOF
SORTS           ANY
SIGNATURE       e: -> ANY
                f: ANY ANY -> ANY
                a: -> ANY
ORDERING        LPO
                f > e > a
VARIABLES       x,y,z : ANY
EQUATIONS       f(x, e) = x
                f(f(x, y), z) = f(x, f(y, z))
CONCLUSION      f(a, e) = a
